menu "BlueAudio Puck: battery"

    config PUCK_BATTERY_ADC_GPIO
        int "Battery sense GPIO (-1 if not fitted)"
        default -1
        range -1 39
        help
            Must be an ADC1 pin: 32-39. ADC2 is shared with the Wi-Fi radio and
            is unavailable whenever Wi-Fi is active, so it is not accepted here
            even though this firmware does not currently use Wi-Fi.

            GPIO 35 is a good choice on a devkit: input-only, so it cannot be
            driven by mistake, and it is rarely used for anything else.

            Left at -1 the firmware reports "USB powered" and never samples.

    config PUCK_BATTERY_DIVIDER_RATIO_X100
        int "Divider ratio, times 100"
        default 200
        range 100 1000
        help
            Cell voltage divided by pin voltage, times 100. Two equal resistors
            give a 2:1 divider, so 200. For other pairs the ratio is
            (R_top + R_bottom) / R_bottom.

            A full Li-po is 4.2 V and the ADC tops out near 3.1 V at 11 dB
            attenuation, so the divider must be at least about 1.4:1. 2:1 with
            two 100k resistors is the usual choice: it fits comfortably and
            draws only ~21 uA.

            Set this to match the resistors you actually fitted. A percentage
            from a wrong ratio is worse than no percentage at all.

    config PUCK_BATTERY_INTERVAL_SECONDS
        int "Seconds between samples"
        default 30
        range 1 600
        help
            Battery voltage moves slowly. Sampling often costs power and makes
            the on-screen percentage jitter with playback load.

    config PUCK_BATTERY_LOW_PERCENT
        int "Warn below this percentage"
        default 20
        range 1 90

    config PUCK_BATTERY_CRITICAL_PERCENT
        int "Treat as critical below this percentage"
        default 5
        range 1 50
        help
            At this level the firmware reports PUCK_BATTERY_CRITICAL so the UI
            can warn. It does not shut down on its own -- cutting the audio out
            from under someone is worse than running the cell a little lower.

endmenu
